                        "source_sense_id": "49be8e8f-c958-3cd8-9057-da15b8f0559e",
                        "target_lang_word": "gullible",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gullible",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2e71207-e0e0-3857-9f69-e326c4fda75f",
                                        "entry_id": "e45ee3f8-21a2-3434-a4e6-2b249dea2b25",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Easily deceived or duped; naive, easily cheated or fooled."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a110d8fd-9f8d-476d-82b7-8ed8b1697759",
                                                "sense_id": "f2e71207-e0e0-3857-9f69-e326c4fda75f",
                                                "text": "Andrew is so gullible, the way he still believes in Santa Claus, the Easter Bunny, the Tooth Fairy, and the Sandman at the age of fourteen."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gullible",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da8f3d64-50fe-38a1-8a32-e4c4c7ad6538",
                                        "entry_id": "37c14882-ba0d-36a0-b21e-4a1ac7c1f4ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gullible person; someone easily fooled or tricked."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2511c913-67fa-467a-b129-5a25c191f72f",
                                                "sense_id": "da8f3d64-50fe-38a1-8a32-e4c4c7ad6538",
                                                "text": "They pictured to these gullibles the unearthly delights that were to be enjoyed as servants of the Spaniards. But such tricks could not last, for Cuba was too close to Saint Domingue, and news of the real conditions leaked across the windward passage and were bruited about."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b73fc4c9-6c68-4678-a1eb-aefed1cc04d2",
                                                "sense_id": "da8f3d64-50fe-38a1-8a32-e4c4c7ad6538",
                                                "text": "Spurious accounts that snare the gullible are readily available. Skeptical treatments are much harder to find."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14001c59-66c6-4d13-a368-7b532a704fa9",
                        "source_entry_id": "973d3fab-25de-3248-b226-a9daa526c36b",
                        "source_sense_id": "49be8e8f-c958-3cd8-9057-da15b8f0559e",
                        "target_lang_word": "credulous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "credulous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3af6086-5cfe-3f07-aa1b-8e21c58ec1b3",
                                        "entry_id": "408b92c0-01a3-3c28-a319-3ffdbecfd664",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessively ready to believe things; gullible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcf0c022-54f9-4247-bec0-61eeadcbafd5",
                                                "sense_id": "c3af6086-5cfe-3f07-aa1b-8e21c58ec1b3",
                                                "text": "[…]purſued his vnneighbourly purpoſe in ſuch ſort: that hee being the ſtronger perſwader, and ſhe (belike) too credulous in beleeuing or elſe ouer-feeble in reſiſting, from priuate imparlance, they fell to action; and continued their cloſe fight a long while together, vnſeene and vvithout ſuſpition, no doubt to their equall ioy and contentment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ed1ab4e-267a-4c66-adde-eabd492b0b8a",
                                                "sense_id": "c3af6086-5cfe-3f07-aa1b-8e21c58ec1b3",
                                                "text": "The doctor was a small, black, plump man with fuzzy hair and round, credulous eyes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b232cae0-f569-30ed-aaa9-7976b37dff89",
                                        "entry_id": "408b92c0-01a3-3c28-a319-3ffdbecfd664",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Believed too readily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ecf0559-45af-4b3e-be7e-5e7b29f771b0",
                                                "sense_id": "b232cae0-f569-30ed-aaa9-7976b37dff89",
                                                "text": "'Twas he possess'd me with your credulous death"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b3e172d-d9dc-4cb6-b455-a97e607bd557",
                                                "sense_id": "b232cae0-f569-30ed-aaa9-7976b37dff89",
                                                "text": "The powerful mind of Aristotle, which led him to reject with disdain the credulous tales and fabulous stories of the age, can nowhere be traced in the writings of Pliny, whose works, on the contrary, abound in fables and in prodigies, at once manifesting that weakness of mind inseparable from credulity, or that disinclination to investigate truth, which is the sure mark of a secondary order of intellect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7d50176-13eb-4084-aa31-0ba55cd4d0aa",
                                                "sense_id": "b232cae0-f569-30ed-aaa9-7976b37dff89",
                                                "text": "The media (and politicians) are replete with credulous stories about machine learning and AI, but these stories are often based on commercial claims."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
